	<key>readme</key>
	<string>Tally logs time by switching tasks.

t             the previous task first (↩ resumes it), the other recent ones, Stop, Today
t parser      Start or Resume parser; matching tasks below
t parser 14:05  start at 14:05 (or -20m, -1h20m); the row says what it ends or cuts
⇧↩            start where the last block ended, filling the gap
t @today      the day as a ribbon, with totals (@yesterday, @week, @month, 2026-10-19)
t bar         install the SwiftBar plugin: the running task in the menu bar
t st ↩        stop (any command word works from two letters: to, yes, we, la, mo, ba)
⌥↩            stop the running task, from any task row
The second hotkey stops the running task without opening Alfred: give it a key.
</string>
